      "math_academy_id": "e-4232",
      "problem": "What is the $5$th term of the geometric sequence given below?\n\n$$\nf(n+1) = -5f(n),\\quad f(1) = -1,\\quad  n\\geq 1\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "We use the recursive formula to compute the terms of the sequence up to the $4$th term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) & =-1 \\\\ f(2) & =-5f(1)=-5(-1)=5 \\\\ f(3) & =-5f(2)=-5(5)=-25 \\\\ f(4) & =-5f(3)=-5(-25)=125 \\\\ f(5) & =-5f(4)=-5(125)=-625\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(5)=-625.$",
